20	// after all validation and merging has run, so the exercise goes through the
21	// real code path — real atomic file writes, real on-disk state afterwards —
22	// without filling a disk or relying on wall-clock timing. The same two nodes
23	// run under both failure positions, so the result cannot depend on which node
24	// happens to be written first (that order is deliberately not promised).
